  }, {
    "id" : "feature-summary-h",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Summary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "cc73387c",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Adds a Currency root entity (code, name, rateToUsd) with save-time uniqueness, format and positive-rate validation, its approved descriptor and form shipped verbatim, and an observer sheet. A CurrencyConverter implements convert over stored rates with 2-decimal rounding and a code-naming error, and an idempotent seed supplies USD, EUR and GBP. The Currencies screen is built from its mock and registered under Reference data › Currencies, in four tasks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "feature-design-h",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 2
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Design"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "5cd4c332",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Currency entity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "32dc82ab",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "New root bean "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "refdata.Currency",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " with three required fields: "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "code",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text, unique, format of exactly 3 letters), "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "name",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (text) and "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "rateToUsd",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " (decimal number, strictly greater than 0). The spec says no existing entity or spec is reused (Dependencies: None), so nothing is re-modelled. The entity descriptor "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "entity_descriptors/refdata.Currency.json",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " and the default form "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "ui/refdata.Currency.js",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " are spec-time artifacts and are copied verbatim into the module. Persistence, the observer sheet, uniqueness (P2 / A1), the 3-letter format and the rateToUsd > 0 rule (P1 / A2) all follow the platform entity pattern. Uniqueness and positivity are enforced on save."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "aeb16263",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Conversion and seed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "75a7001c",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "convert(amount, fromCode, toCode)",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " is a domain operation over stored Currency rows, not a new entity. It looks both codes up by "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "code",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " and returns amount × rateToUsd(from) ÷ rateToUsd(to), rounded to 2 decimals (R1, A3: 100 EUR → GBP = 85.04). Rounding uses BigDecimal HALF_UP on the final result only. An unknown code is refused with an error whose message contains that code (R2, A4). A seed applies USD 1.0, EUR 1.08 and GBP 1.27 (R3, A5). The seed is idempotent: it skips codes that already exist, so it cannot trip the unique rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "id" : "7ec88638",
    "type" : "heading",
    "props" : {
      "level" : 3
    },
    "content" : [ {
